<title>BOLIVIA: SOCCER-BRAZIL BEAT COSTA RICA 5-0 IN COPA AMERICA.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BRAZIL BEAT COSTA RICA 5-0 IN COPA AMERICA.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA CRUZ, Bolivia 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil beat Costa</p>
<p>Rica 5-0 (halftime 2-0) in a Copa America first round group C</p>
<p>match on Friday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Djalminha (23rd minute), Ronald Gonzalez (35, own goal),</p>
<p>Ronaldo (48 and 49), Romario (60)</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points)</p>
<p> Brazil	 1  1  0  0  5  0  3</p>
<p> Mexico	 1  1  0  0  2  1  3</p>
<p> Colombia     1  0  0  1  1  2  0</p>
<p> Costa Rica   1  0  0  1  0  5  0</p>
<p>Note: top two teams in each group plus the two</p>
<p>third-placed teams with the best records qualify for the</p>
<p>quarter-finals.</p>
</text>
